From c2e92aeb5494516bd7e86753b88023201751e76f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 05:10:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add RFI module + side-by-side bid comparison matrix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Gap-fill pass driven by the construction mind-map audit. Two of the
highest-leverage missing/partial features, built end-to-end against the
existing Firestore backend and conventions:

RFI workflow (new cross-portal module — the audit's biggest single gap,
referenced by the GC, Designer, and Sub branches of the mind map):
- projects/{projectId}/rfis subcollection + firestore.rules (subs/designers/GC
  raise + read; GC/designers answer + close; creators edit their own)
- types/rfi.ts, lib/rfi/firestore.ts (subscribe/create/answer/close/reopen),
  reusable role-aware RFIPanel with create + answer/close modals
- Surfaces: GC project page (/projects/:id/rfis) + project sidebar item,
  Designer Portal "RFIs" tab, Subcontractor Portal "RFIs" tab (project picker)
- Answer fires a notification to the original author via the shared pipeline

Bid comparison matrix (finishes a partial feature — existing panel only had a
per-sub summary; the GC leveling view was missing):
- BidComparisonMatrix.tsx: subs as columns, line items as rows, per-row low/high
  highlighting, spread %, compliance flags, award-from-table
- Summary/Compare toggle wired into the canonical PortalBidsPanel

No changes to existing collections. tsc clean for all new/edited files.
